DESCRIPTION:Alaikadal (meaning "the deep sea") is a powerful dance-theatre production inspired by the lives of South India's traditional coastal fishing communities. Through movement\, music and evocative storytelling\, director and choreographer Junafar Juno\, himself from a fishing community\, brings to the stage stories of labour\, survival and belonging that are rarely documented\, honouring a way of life sustained through collective effort and an enduring relationship with nature.
DTEND:20260822T140000Z
DTSTART:20260822T130000Z
SUMMARY:Alaikadal
UID:1378@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/alaikadal/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://map-india.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Untitled-design-17.jpg
CATEGORIES:Guided Walk,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20260807T144137Z
DESCRIPTION:Folio from a ragamala series: Desakh Ragini\, Unknown\, Late 19th Century\, Opaque watercolour on paper\, H. 28.5 cm\, W. 20.4 cm\, Jaipur\, Rajasthan\, India\, PTG.01140\nJoin Aayati Sengupta\, Curator of Grip\, Hold\, Pin\, for the first walkthrough of the exhibition. Through a close reading of the works on view\, the walkthrough will explore wrestling as more than a sport—as a site where discipline\, kinship\, identity and everyday life converge. Drawing on photography\, archival material and moving image\, Grip\, Hold\, Pin traces the histories and lived experiences that shape wrestling cultures across India\, inviting audiences to consider the relationships between body\, labour\, tradition and representation. 
DTEND:20260815T070000Z
DTSTART:20260815T060000Z
SUMMARY:Curator walkthrough - Grip\, Hold\, Pin
